jobDescription:
&lt;p&gt;At Celigo, we believe integration should empower — not exhaust — innovation. As a modern Integration and Automation Platform (iPaaS), we’re on a mission to simplify how companies integrate, automate, and optimize processes. Powered by game-changing technology like runtime AI and prebuilt, mission-critical integrations, Celigo is redefining how businesses connect their world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Celigo is looking for an IT Systems Engineer who will be primarily responsible for engineering IT solutions. The IT Engineer will be solving incoming help desk questions handling level 1 and 2 tickets. This person would liaise with third-party support to assist in using cloud-based services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would you do if hired?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and support scalable IT solutions, including SSO expansion, onboarding and offboarding automation, and other global automation initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and maintain core IT infrastructure while contributing to a strong security posture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle Level 1 and Level 2 IT tickets for the US, EMEA, and Philippines regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide on-site IT support at the India HQ during the afternoon hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support onboarding and offboarding processes across the US, EMEA, and PH, including IT Orientation Calls on Mondays.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform system migrations and tool transitions as needed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Celigo’s integrator.io platform to automate internal IT workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build self-service solutions to reduce ticket volume and improve employee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain clear IT documentation and runbooks to support global teams and reduce repeat issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally to improve efficiency and IT service delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a regional bridge between global IT teams by ensuring consistent processes, documentation, and handoffs across the US, EMEA, PH, and India&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who are we looking for?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;B.E/B.Tech in Computer Science with 3-5 years of hands-on experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.E or B.Tech in Computer Science with 3 to 5 years of hands-on IT experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to work a later shift, approximately 1:30 PM to 10:30 PM IST&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering Google Workspace and supporting Google tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with tools such as JAMF, Intune, MS Office, Zoom, Slack, LastPass, and Jira or JSM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with security checks or audits, including CIS benchmarks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with automation scripting and API-based workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting skills across macOS and Windows environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for technology with a proactive, self-driven approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator with strong interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized, adaptable, and comfortable working in a fast-paced, global environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with globally distributed teams and managing handoffs across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here you’ll experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible, hybrid work culture that values autonomy, collaboration, and trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A fast-paced, high-growth environment where innovation and ownership are encouraged at every level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous learning and upskilling opportunities through internal training, mentorship, and global collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional teammates who bring passion, purpose, and creativity to everything they do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A supportive, inclusive workplace that celebrates diverse ideas and perspectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health insurance coverage for employees and dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous leave benefits, including paid time off, wellness days, and parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognition programs and career growth opportunities designed to help you thrive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern office spaces that promote connection, collaboration, and fun.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity, Inclusion, and Accessibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a company, one of the values we hold most dear is fostering a safe, collaborative environment to bring out the best in us, so we created our Taking a Stand Initiative. Our TAS initiative is a volunteer committee open to all Celigans, with representation from underrepresented voices within our company. We believe, unequivocally, that everyone deserves to be in a place where they feel welcome as they are. Learn more about&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.celigo.com/about-us/dei/&quot;&gt; Taking a Stand&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Celigo is proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. We are committed to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, military and veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5 style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integration meets Innovation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;At Celigo, we believe integration should empower — not exhaust — innovation. As a modern Integration and Automation Platform (iPaaS), we’re on a mission to simplify how companies integrate, automate, and optimize processes. Powered by game-changing technology like runtime AI and prebuilt, mission-critical integrations, Celigo is redefining how businesses connect their world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Join a team of highly talented individuals committed to offering the best quality services and products in the area of business cloud computing (SaaS). As an &lt;strong&gt;AWS System Development Engineer-1&lt;/strong&gt;, you will design and develop backend features for our integrator.io platform using cutting-edge AWS technologies. Your role will focus on creating scalable, secure, and high-performance systems that enable seamless integrations between business applications like NetSuite, Salesforce.com, Google, Amazon, Magento, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would you do if hired?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design &amp;amp; Development:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, implement, and maintain backend services and APIs using Node.js and JavaScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AWS services (e.g., Lambda, EC2, S3, DynamoDB, CloudFormation) to build scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance application performance, reliability, and security through continuous monitoring and optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues in production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DevOps &amp;amp; Automation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and integrate automated deployment pipelines using CI/CD best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with DevOps teams to ensure smooth system integrations and continuous delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Documentation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside product, operations, and design teams to translate business requirements into technical specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear documentation of system architectures, code, and development processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay updated on the latest AWS technologies and industry trends, applying new knowledge to improve our platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-7 years of hands-on experience in software development, preferably in a cloud-based or product-driven environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in JavaScript and Node.js development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid hands-on experience with AWS services (Lambda, EC2, S3, DynamoDB, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with RESTful API design and microservices architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Competencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with version control systems (e.g., Git) and CI/CD pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of containerization technologies like Docker is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills and an ability to quickly learn and adapt to new technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Educational Background:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
